# Component Library UI Composition

Search `component-library` for existing primitives before adding generic UI. Compose (`Popup` + `ViewSwitch` + `Media`, etc.) rather than building domain mega-components.

- Follow library idioms: HOC state/display split, children cloning, namespaced injected props.
- Exception: data-template iterators (`Grid`, `VirtualGrid`, `Masonry`, `Map`) inject the datum as top-level `item`/`index` so one card template works under any of them. Controller contracts (`fold`, `mediaLightbox`, `tabs`, `viewSwitch`) stay namespaced.
- Cross-app reusable compositions → small library wrappers with slots/children for domain content.
- Domain workflows (rename, delete, crop, variants, notes, entity links) stay in the owning app.
